Worth flagging as an example of this report's own "single run, not averaged" caveat: the N=10 library-backed cell dropped from 10.85ms (double) / 1.53ms (single) in the previous revision of this report to 0.11ms / 0.21ms here - the same code, the same machine, no explanation found beyond ordinary single-run timing noise at sub-millisecond scale (background scheduling, turbo/frequency-scaling state at the moment of the call). Not investigated further; the N=50/N=100 cells are far more consistent between runs and are the more trustworthy numbers here. EigDecompose was deliberately not benchmarked at N=1000 - PurePascalEigHqr2's QR-iteration has a materially larger constant factor than the LU-based Invert/LinearSolve fallbacks, so N=1000 there would take disproportionately longer for comparatively little extra insight; see newVMbench.lpr's own header comment.\par
